    {
      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>A care home is a workplace and a home. The ordinary hazards hurt frail people fastest: a wet floor, an overdue hoist check, a wedged fire door, an unflushed tap. A safety audit walks the whole home and records each control. The question is how to record it so nothing is lost before the write-up.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>A care home has duties under the Health and Safety at Work etc Act 1974.</li><li>Falls and moving and handling are the commonest sources of harm.</li><li>Hoists and slings need thorough examination under LOLER 1998. The audit checks it is in date.</li><li>Legionella and fire (RRFSO 2005) are premises risks.</li><li>The registered manager owns the actions.</li><li>Quickler records the walk and the evidence. It is not a care record.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The duty",
      "heading": "Health and safety in a care home",
      "html": "<p>A care home has duties as an employer and as the person in charge of the premises. It must assess risks to residents, staff and visitors, and put controls in place. The audit checks those controls are working.</p>"
